   "answer": "仅根据当前导入的这份课件，**无法给出**本地 StudyGraph 服务今天的实际 P95 响应时间。\n\n**原因说明：**\n当前课件（Advanced AI Computing and Systems）的内容仅涉及计算机体系结构中的内存层次结构（CPU/GPU Memory Hierarchy）、平均内存访问时间（AMAT）、缓存命中/未命中（Hit/Miss）以及 GPU 内存银行冲突（Bank Conflicts）等概念 [S1, S2, S3]。课件中**不包含**任何关于 StudyGraph 服务性能指标、响应时间统计（如 P95、P99）或具体日期（“今天”）的数据。\n\n因此，基于现有材料，该问题无法回答。",
   "citations": [
    {
     "document_id": "ad66f2c8360da43ea0981bffa549956185949044062a0abe4689381ced423402",
     "chunk_id": "ad66f2c8360da43ea0981bffa549956185949044062a0abe4689381ced423402-p26-1",
     "page": 26,
     "text": "CPU Memory Hierarchy\n\nAverage Memory Access Time (AMAT)\n\n  AMAT = Hit time + Miss rate x Miss penalty\n  Miss Penalty: time to fetch a block from lower memory\n  level\n   Access Time: Latency for the memory to handle one access\n    Transfer Time: Latency to transfer data block to higher level\n   Miss penalty = access time + data size / bandwidth\n\n\n\n\n\n A cache helps when common hits remain fast and sufficiently few accesses pay\n▪\n  the miss penalty.\n\n\nMemory Wall     CPU Memory    GPU Memory    SOTA Memory     Advanced AI Computing and Systems        26",
     "preview_url": "/api/documents/ad66f2c8360da43ea0981bffa549956185949044062a0abe4689381ced423402/pages/26/preview",
     "source": "S1"
    },
    {
     "document_id": "ad66f2c8360da43ea0981bffa549956185949044062a0abe4689381ced423402",
     "chunk_id": "ad66f2c8360da43ea0981bffa549956185949044062a0abe4689381ced423402-p25-1",
     "page": 25,
     "text": "CPU Memory Hierarchy\n\nHit or Miss of Caches: Benefit vs. Penalty\n   Hit: The requested memory block is       Miss: The requested memory block\n  found in the current cache level, with         is not present in the current cache\n  a valid tag match.                              level, so it must be retrieved from the\n                                           next lower level.    Hit Rate: Hits / Total Accesses\n                                          Miss Rate: 1 - Hit Rate   Cache Read/Write: Find the data on\n   cache and then perform read/write        Miss Penalty: The additional time\n                                              required to service a miss\n\n\n\n\n\nMemory Wall     CPU Memory    GPU Memory    SOTA Memory     Advanced AI Computing and Systems        25",
     "preview_url": "/api/documents/ad66f2c8360da43ea0981bffa549956185949044062a0abe4689381ced423402/pages/25/preview",
     "source": "S2"
    },
    {
     "document_id": "ad66f2c8360da43ea0981bffa549956185949044062a0abe4689381ced423402",
     "chunk_id": "ad66f2c8360da43ea0981bffa549956185949044062a0abe4689381ced423402-p51-1",
     "page": 51,
     "text": "GPU Memory Hierarchy\n\nAccess Memory: Bank Conflicts Serialize Otherwise Parallel\nAccesses\n\n\n\n\n\n▪ Typical GPUs use 32 banks; the figure shows 8 for readability. Same-address\n  reads can use broadcast.\n▪ Different addresses in the same bank require multiple service rounds. This differs\n  from global-memory coalescing.\n\nMemory Wall     CPU Memory    GPU Memory    SOTA Memory     Advanced AI Computing and Systems        51",
